    {
      "id": "overview-sticky",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Day 39 Solution: AI Memory, Context & RAG\n\nThree parts in one file.\n\n**1. Memory:** a webhook feeds an AI Agent with **Simple Memory**, keyed by `conversation_id`, so the agent remembers earlier turns of the same conversation.\n\n**2. Load the knowledge base (run once):** click *Execute workflow* on **Load Knowledge Base**. The text is split into chunks, turned into embeddings and stored in the **In-Memory Vector Store** under the key `course_knowledge_base`.\n\n**3. Ask questions (RAG):** a webhook feeds a second AI Agent whose only tool is that vector store, so it answers from your text and cites it.\n\n**Credentials needed to run for real:** OpenAI API key (Chat Model and Embeddings nodes).\n\n**Reference:** WEEK_06_AI_AGENTS/DAILY_TASKS/DAY_39_AI_Memory_and_Context.md",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 460
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "memory-persistence-note",
      "name": "Memory Persistence Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        740,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Note: what survives a restart\n\nSimple Memory and the In-Memory Vector Store both live in n8n's RAM. They work across requests while n8n is running, but **a restart (or a Render free-tier sleep) wipes them**: re-run *Load Knowledge Base* afterwards. For production, swap Simple Memory for Postgres or Redis Chat Memory, and the in-memory store for Postgres PGVector, Supabase or Pinecone.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 360
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "memory-chat-trigger",
      "name": "Memory Chat Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "ai-memory",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "memory-chat-agent",
      "name": "Memory Chat Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        520,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.body.message }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a helpful assistant. Recall any facts the user has already told you in this conversation."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "memory-chat-model",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
